hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16392","He said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, or Badr, I doubt, from Talq ibn 'Ali al-Hanafi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his backbone between its bowing and its prostration."
"16393","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ali ibn Shayban, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at a man who does not straighten his backbone between his bowing and his prostration."
"16394","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Mulazim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer in a single garment, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loosed his waist-wrapper and crossed it with his cloak, then stood and prayed. So when he finished the prayer, he said: Each of you finds two garments."
"16395","He said: Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us perform ablution when he touches his penis? He said: It is only a piece of you, or of your body."
"16396","He said: Yunus narrated to us: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Isa ibn Khuthaym, from Qays ibn Talq, that his father witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man asked him about prayer in a single garment, and he said nothing to him. So when the prayer was established, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crossed between his two garments and prayed in them."
"16397","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wants his wife for a need, let him come to her, even if she is at the oven."
"16398","He said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from 'Ali ibn Talq, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are not two witrs in a night. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man praying in a single garment. He said: And each of you finds two garments."
"16399","Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break fast, and if it is obscured to you, complete the number."
"16400","He said: Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Nu'man, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dawn is not the tall one in the horizon, but it is the transverse red one."
"16401","He said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man asked him and said: I touched my private part, or: a man touches his private part in prayer, is ablution due upon him? He said: No, it is only a part of you."
"16402","He said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from Talq ibn Ali, he said: We came as a delegation to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when he bade us farewell he commanded me, so I brought him a small waterskin of water, and he scooped from it, then spat in it three times, then closed its mouth, then said: Go with it and sprinkle the mosque of your people with it, and command them to raise their heads when Allah raises it. I said: The land between us and you is distant and it will dry up. He said: Then when it dries, extend it."
"16403","He said: Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir informed us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, made these crescents time-marks for people, so fast at its sighting and break fast at its sighting, and if it is obscured from you then complete the number."
"16404","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, should one of us perform ablution if he touches his private part in prayer? He said: Is it anything but a part of you, or a piece of flesh of you."
"16405","He said: Affan narrated to us, Mulazim ibn Amr al-Suhaymi narrated to us, my grandfather Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: And Siraj ibn Uqba narrated to me that Qays ibn Talq narrated to them both that his father Talq ibn Ali came to us in Ramadan and stayed with us until evening, and he led us in the night prayer in Ramadan and led us in witr, then he went down to the mosque of Rayman and prayed with them until only the witr remained, so he put a man forward and he led them in witr, and he said: I heard the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There are no two witrs in one night."
